window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-0d81218eacd2463c"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"build-plugins\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"_1\">构建插件</h1> <blockquote> <p>完整文档索引请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。如需查看文档的 Markdown 版本，可在页面 URL 末尾追加 <code>.md</code>。</p> </blockquote> <p>将经常重复的工作流程变成可在 ChatGPT 中重复使用的插件。通过对话描述任务，补充所需的指令和参考资料，然后测试并不断完善结果。</p> <p><strong>自定义 GPT 正在迁移为插件</strong></p> <p>ChatGPT Enterprise 中的自定义 GPT 将逐步退役。如果你使用自定义 GPT，请按照<a href=\"#/article/a-866d18fe9ed30c97\">将自定义 GPT 工作流程迁移到插件</a>中的说明迁移、测试并分享替代方案。也可以按照下方步骤从头创建插件，或编辑现有插件。</p> <p><a id=\"what-is-a-plugin\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">什么是插件？</h2> <p>插件是一种可重复使用的软件包，可帮助 ChatGPT 完成某项任务。插件可以包含应用、技能，也可以两者兼有。</p> <blockquote> <p>插图：插件可以包含应用、技能，或两者兼有。应用连接你的工具；技能指导工作如何完成。</p> </blockquote> <p><a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/11487775\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">应用（需联网）</a>可将 ChatGPT 连接到其他服务。<a href=\"#/article/a-f06621b97709dae2?anchor=use-skills-for-repeatable-work\">技能</a>则为任务提供指令，例如以一致的格式总结文档。</p> <ul> <li><strong>查找文档（应用）：</strong> 在你有权访问的已连接服务中搜索文件。</li> <li><strong>总结文档（技能）：</strong> 将你提供的文档整理成概览、要点和待解决问题。</li> <li><strong>使用模板（技能）：</strong> 按标准格式组织你提供的信息。</li> <li><strong>比较文档（应用 + 技能）：</strong> 通过获准的应用检索你有权访问的两份文档，再按清单进行比较。</li> </ul> <p>插件名称可以是某项服务的名称（例如 Google Drive），也可以是某个工作流程的名称（例如 Document Summary）。查看插件详情，了解其中包含的内容。</p> <p>你可以通过向 ChatGPT 描述需求来创建插件。本指南介绍的步骤不需要编写代码。</p> <p><a id=\"before-you-start\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">开始之前</h2> <p>以下步骤适用于已在工作区启用插件创建和编辑功能的 ChatGPT 网页版。你可以在 Chat 或 Work 中通过对话完成创建和编辑。</p> <p>先准备一个明确的任务、一个理想结果示例，以及插件可能要用到的参考文件。如果工作流程需要某个应用，请确认该应用在你的工作区中获准使用，并完成必要的连接设置。插件不会因此获得对该应用文件、数据或操作的额外访问权限。</p> <p><strong>所需权限</strong></p> <p>你需要 <strong>使用插件（Use plugins）</strong> 权限，并且工作区中必须提供 Plugin Creator。要编辑现有插件，你还需要编辑权限。工作区插件的创建者以及工作区所有者或管理员都可以编辑它。</p> <p><a id=\"using-a-plugin\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">使用插件</h2> <p>如果希望 ChatGPT 在 Chat 或 Work 中遵循某个工作流程或使用其应用，可以使用已安装的插件。输入 <strong>@</strong> 并选择该插件。</p> <ol> <li>在 ChatGPT 中开始新对话。</li> <li>在消息框中输入 <strong>@</strong>，然后开始键入插件名称。</li> <li>在菜单的 <strong>Plugins</strong> 下选择该插件。</li> <li>描述你的需求，添加相关文件，然后发送消息。</li> </ol> <blockquote> <p>插图：ChatGPT Work 的 @ 菜单展示了 FAQ Practice Coach 插件；输入 @faq 后，菜单中还会单独显示 Skills 区域。</p> </blockquote> <p><em>ChatGPT Work 中的 @ 菜单会显示匹配的插件和技能。在 <strong>Plugins</strong> 下选择一个插件。</em></p> <p>如果插件需要连接应用，请按提示完成连接。若要查找并安装插件，请参阅 <a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\">Plugins</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"create-a-plugin-from-scratch\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">从头创建插件</h2> <p>从一项经常执行的任务和一个清晰的理想结果示例开始。Plugin Creator 会通过对话帮你把需求整理成可重复使用的工作流程：你可以说明步骤、添加模板或参考文件，并根据需要逐步调整。下面的书面示例以“文档总结”插件为例，用来生成概览、要点和待解决问题。你可以将同样的方法用于其他任务。</p> <p><a href=\"https://cdn.openai.com/devhub/docs/codex/build-plugins/create-plugin-2x-hq.webm\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">插件创建示例：提交初始请求后，Plugin Creator 给出第一条回复；视频以原始速度的两倍播放。（需联网）</a></p> <p>此视频展示了如何首次提出插件创建请求，以及 Plugin Creator 的第一条回复。下方的文字示例使用的是另一个工作流程。</p> <p><a id=\"step-1-mention-plugin-creator\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"1-plugin-creator\">第 1 步：提及 Plugin Creator</h3> <p>在 Chat 或 ChatGPT Work 中开始对话。输入 <strong>@</strong>，搜索 <strong>Plugin Creator</strong>，然后从菜单中选择它。</p> <p><a id=\"step-2-describe-the-workflow\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"2\">第 2 步：描述工作流程</h3> <p>好的创建提示应给 Plugin Creator 一份实用的任务说明：</p> <ul> <li><strong>目的：</strong> 说明要重复执行的任务，以及你会在什么情况下使用该插件。</li> <li><strong>输入：</strong> 说明你会提供哪些信息，以及插件应如何使用每个附件。</li> <li><strong>输出：</strong> 说明结果面向谁，并指定格式、长度和语气；最好附上示例。</li> <li><strong>规则：</strong> 说明必须执行的步骤、哪些内容需要你审核，以及遇到信息缺失时如何处理。例如，可以要求插件提问，或将字段标注为“未说明”。</li> </ul> <p>要求生成可以配合新输入重复使用的指令。对于某次任务特有的细节（例如某份具体文档），应明确标记为测试示例。</p> <p><strong>从头创建插件：</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Create a plugin called Document Summary. Summarize documents I provide in three sections: Overview, Key points, and Open questions. Use the attached template for the format. Base the summary only on the document. If requested information is missing, mark it as not provided. Do not edit the source document.\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">创建一个名为 Document Summary 的插件。将我提供的文档总结为三个部分：Overview（概览）、Key points（要点）和 Open questions（待解答问题）。格式使用所附模板。摘要只能依据文档内容。如果所需信息缺失，就标为未提供。不要编辑源文档。</div></div> <p><a id=\"step-3-add-context-and-refine-the-instructions\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"3\">第 3 步：添加上下文并完善指令</h3> <p>附上插件应使用的模板、示例或参考文件。回答 Plugin Creator 的问题，并要求它持续修改，直到指令符合任务要求。如果工作流程需要应用，请说明任务中的哪一部分依赖它。</p> <p>第一版应聚焦于一个工作流程。清晰的名称和说明有助于你和团队成员识别插件的用途。</p> <p><a id=\"step-4-review-and-finish-creating-the-plugin\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"4\">第 4 步：检查并完成插件创建</h3> <p>按照 Plugin Creator 的提示完成创建。在使用插件之前，请检查它的名称、说明、指令和参考资料。</p> <p>新建的工作区插件默认是私有的，因此你可以先进行测试，再分享给他人。</p> <p><a id=\"include-apps-in-your-plugin\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_6\">在插件中加入应用</h2> <p>应用可以将 ChatGPT 连接到其他服务，例如文件存储或项目管理工具。根据应用及其启用的功能，ChatGPT 可能可以搜索或读取信息，也可能执行某些操作（例如创建文档或更新记录）。技能说明如何完成工作；应用则提供完成工作所需的信息或操作能力。</p> <p>应用是可选的。“文档总结”可以处理你粘贴的文本或附加的文件。如果你希望工作流程从其他服务检索文档或执行受支持的操作，再加入相应应用。</p> <p><a id=\"find-apps-available-to-you\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_7\">查找可供你使用的应用</h3> <p>在计划创建和使用插件的工作区中浏览：</p> <ol> <li>在 ChatGPT 中打开 <strong>Plugins</strong>。搜索所需服务，或浏览以你的工作区命名的选项卡。</li> <li>打开插件详情并查看其中的 <strong>Apps</strong> 区域。插件名称可能与其连接的服务相同，但有些插件只包含技能。</li> <li>检查所包含应用的功能和连接状态。如果显示 <strong>Disabled by admin</strong> 或 <strong>Admin approval required</strong>，请向工作区管理员申请访问权限。</li> </ol> <p>如果你的账户显示的是 <strong>Apps</strong> 而不是 <strong>Plugins</strong>，请在那里浏览可用连接。目录中出现某个插件，并不表示它包含的所有应用都已可用。</p> <p>记下应用名称及其支持的功能，然后告诉 Plugin Creator 你希望如何使用它。有关浏览和设置的更多信息，请参阅 <a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a?anchor=use-and-install-plugins\">Plugins</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"add-an-app-to-your-workflow\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_8\">将应用加入工作流程</h3> <p>创建或编辑插件时：</p> <ol> <li><strong>选择可用应用。</strong> 使用工作区允许、且你有权使用的应用。如果应用不可用，请向工作区管理员申请访问权限。</li> <li><strong>说明应用要做什么。</strong> 告诉 Plugin Creator 应加入哪个应用、要读取什么信息或执行什么操作，以及你希望先检查哪些内容。</li> <li><strong>连接并检查。</strong> 按提示完成设置并检查所请求的权限。你可能需要登录；某些应用使用管理员管理的连接。检查完成后的插件所包含的应用，然后用你已能访问的信息进行测试。</li> </ol> <p>在下例中，请将 <strong>[app name]</strong> 替换为工作区允许使用的应用名称。</p> <p><strong>加入一个应用：</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Include [app name] in Document Summary, if it’s available to me. Read the document I link to and draft the Overview, Key points, and Open questions in chat. Keep the rule about marking missing information. Do not create or edit files in the app. If you cannot access the document, ask me to attach it.\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">如果 [app name] 对我可用，就将它加入 Document Summary。阅读我链接的文档，并在聊天中起草 Overview（概览）、Key points（要点）和 Open questions（待解答问题）。保留标记缺失信息的规则。不要在该应用中创建或编辑文件。如果无法访问文档，请让我将它作为附件提供。</div></div> <p>加入应用不会授予新的访问权限。工作区中的应用和操作设置、连接权限，以及你在源服务中的访问权限仍然适用。使用该插件的团队成员也必须拥有所需的应用访问权限并完成连接设置。</p> <p><a id=\"connect-a-custom-mcp-server\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"mcp\">连接自定义 MCP 服务器</h3> <p>如果现有应用无法满足你的工作流程，可以<a href=\"#/article/a-dd3c07a3ae6aafeb?anchor=build-an-mcp-plugin\">使用自定义 MCP 服务器连接工具</a>。你可以使用 Plugin Creator 和 Sites 构建连接到自己系统的插件。</p> <p><a id=\"test-your-plugin\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_9\">测试插件</h2> <p>如果系统提示安装插件，请先安装，然后开始新对话。输入 <strong>@</strong> 并选择插件，再交给它一项你熟悉的任务。对于“文档总结”插件，可以提供一份你熟悉的文档并要求它总结。</p> <p>检查结果是否符合指定格式、是否使用了正确的参考资料，以及是否指出了信息缺失之处。然后再提供一份细节缺失或含糊的文档，检查总结是否能指出这些问题。</p> <p>如果插件使用了应用，请检查它是否能访问任务所需的信息或执行所需操作。如果你计划在 Chat 和 Work 中都使用它，请分别测试；不同环境中可用的工具和应用可能不同。</p> <p>修改插件后，保留几个示例提示供你重复测试。</p> <blockquote> <p>插图：创建插件、使用真实示例测试、编辑指令或文件，然后再次测试；根据需要重复编辑和测试，检查结果后再分享。</p> </blockquote> <p><em>分享前先测试；每次更新后都应重新进行检查。</em></p> <p><a id=\"edit-an-existing-plugin\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_10\">编辑现有插件</h2> <p><a id=\"step-1-open-the-plugin-for-editing\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"1\">第 1 步：打开插件进行编辑</h3> <p>打开 <strong>Plugins</strong>，选择要修改的插件，然后选择 <strong>Edit Plugin</strong>。系统会打开用于更新插件的对话。</p> <p><a id=\"step-2-describe-what-should-change\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"2_1\">第 2 步：描述要做的修改</h3> <p>好的编辑提示应说明需要改变的行为或参考文件、希望达到的结果，以及哪些内容必须保留。如果结果不符合预期，请附上该结果并说明你原本期望看到什么。可以要求用熟悉的输入生成一个示例，便于前后对照。</p> <p>请明确你要更新的是可重复使用的插件指令，还是只修改某一次结果。替换参考文件时，请指出旧文件，并说明新文件应如何使用。</p> <p>例如，要更改输出：</p> <p><strong>更新输出：</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Update Document Summary so Key points appears in a table with Point and Source columns. In Source, identify the supporting passage or section when available. Keep Overview, Open questions, and the rule about marking missing information. Show me a sample result from this document.\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">更新 Document Summary，让 Key points（要点）以表格显示，包含 Point（要点）和 Source（来源）两列。在 Source 中，能确定时就指出支持该要点的段落或章节。保留 Overview（概览）、Open questions（待解答问题）以及标记缺失信息的规则。用这份文档展示一个示例结果。</div></div> <p>要替换参考资料：</p> <p><strong>替换参考资料：</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Replace the existing summary template with the attached revised template. Keep the other reference files and instructions unchanged. Tell me what you changed, then help me test it with this document.\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">用附件中的修订版模板替换现有摘要模板。其他参考文件和指令保持不变。告诉我修改了什么，然后帮助我用这份文档测试。</div></div> <p><a id=\"step-3-review-the-update\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"3_1\">第 3 步：检查更新</h3> <p>检查修改后的指令和文件，然后按照提示完成更新。确认所请求的修改已落实，同时仍保留你需要的内容。</p> <p><a id=\"step-4-test-again\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"4_1\">第 4 步：再次测试</h3> <p>开始新对话并重复使用已保存的测试提示。确认更新后的行为符合预期，也检查你希望保留的部分是否仍然正常。如果其他人也会使用插件，可以请团队成员在广泛采用之前测试一个有代表性的任务。</p> <p><a id=\"share-the-plugin-with-your-team\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_11\">与团队分享插件</h2> <p>插件准备好后，使用其分享设置选择目标人员或群组。分享插件需要 <strong>Share plugins</strong> 权限。将插件发布到工作区目录需要 <strong>Publish plugins to workspace</strong> 权限。</p> <p>分享和安装是两件不同的事。接收者需要自行安装插件，除非管理员已替他们安装。如果工作流程使用某个应用，每个人也都需要相应的应用访问权限和账户连接。</p> <p>在分享时附上一条示例提示和插件链接，并告知团队成员由谁负责维护。有关安装和使用的更多信息，请参阅 <a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\">Plugins</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"if-you-cannot-create-or-edit-a-plugin\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_12\">如果无法创建或编辑插件</h2> <p>先确认你位于预期的工作区。如果没有创建选项或插件编辑器，请联系工作区管理员，确认该功能是否已开放，以及你是否具有所需访问权限。</p> <p>如果团队成员可以打开插件却无法使用，请分别检查插件是否已安装、工作区是否授予了使用插件的权限，以及成员是否能访问所需应用。如果管理员询问如何设置，可参阅 <a href=\"#/article/a-20bc98306a44b420\">Plugin controls</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"continue-with-the-builder-documentation\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_13\">继续阅读构建插件的开发者文档</h2> <p>如需自定义集成或开发插件文件，请参阅<a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/plugins/build/plugins.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">打包插件</a>。<a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/plugins/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">开发者文档（本地尚未收录）</a>介绍了技能和 MCP 服务器的构建、<a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/plugins/build/extensions.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">扩展</a>、测试和公开提交。</p> <p>如需通过 GitHub 在工作区内分发插件，请参阅 <a href=\"#/article/a-ab115ea47731f92a\">Plugin management</a>。</p>","en":"<h1 id=\"build-plugins\">Build plugins</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <p>Turn a workflow you repeat into a plugin you can use again in ChatGPT. Describe the task in a conversation, add the instructions and reference material it needs, then test and refine the result.</p> <p><strong>Custom GPTs are moving to plugins</strong></p> <p>Custom GPTs in ChatGPT Enterprise are being retired. If you use a custom GPT, follow <a href=\"#/article/a-866d18fe9ed30c97\">Moving your custom GPT workflows to plugins</a> to migrate, test, and share its replacement. Use the steps below to create a new plugin from scratch or edit an existing one.</p> <h2 id=\"what-is-a-plugin\">What is a plugin?</h2> <p>A plugin is a reusable package that helps ChatGPT do a task. It can include apps, skills, or both.</p> <blockquote> <p>Illustration: A plugin can contain apps, skills, or both. Apps connect your tools. Skills guide the work.</p> </blockquote> <p><a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/11487775\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Apps (online)</a> connect ChatGPT to other services. <a href=\"#/article/a-f06621b97709dae2?anchor=use-skills-for-repeatable-work\">Skills</a> provide instructions for a task, such as summarizing a document in a consistent format.</p> <ul> <li><strong>Find a document (app):</strong> Search a connected service for a file you have access to.</li> <li><strong>Summarize a document (skill):</strong> Turn a document you provide into an overview, key points, and open questions.</li> <li><strong>Use a template (skill):</strong> Organize information you provide into a standard format.</li> <li><strong>Compare documents (app + skill):</strong> Retrieve two documents you can access through an allowed app, then compare them using your checklist.</li> </ul> <p>Plugins may be named after a service, like Google Drive, or a workflow, like Document Summary. Check the plugin’s details to see what it includes.</p> <p>You can create a plugin by describing what you need in ChatGPT. The steps in this guide do not require code.</p> <h2 id=\"before-you-start\">Before you start</h2> <p>These steps cover ChatGPT on the web when plugin creation and editing are enabled in your workspace. You can create and edit through a conversation in Chat or Work.</p> <p>Have a specific task in mind, an example of a good result, and any reference files the plugin should use. If it needs an app, check that the app is allowed in your workspace and complete any required connection setup. A plugin does not give you additional access to that app's files, data, or actions.</p> <p><strong>Permissions you need</strong></p> <p>You need <strong>Use plugins</strong> permission, and Plugin Creator must be available in your workspace. To edit an existing plugin, you also need edit access. A workspace plugin’s creator and workspace owners or admins can edit it.</p> <h2 id=\"using-a-plugin\">Using a plugin</h2> <p>Use an installed plugin in Chat or Work when you want ChatGPT to follow its workflow or use its apps. Select it with an <strong>@ mention</strong> to choose the plugin for your task.</p> <ol> <li>Start a new conversation in ChatGPT.</li> <li>Type <strong>@</strong> in the message box, then begin typing the plugin’s name.</li> <li>Select the plugin under <strong>Plugins</strong> in the menu.</li> <li>Describe what you need, add any relevant files, and send your message.</li> </ol> <blockquote> <p>Illustration: ChatGPT Work’s @ menu showing FAQ Practice Coach under Plugins and a separate Skills section after entering @faq.</p> </blockquote> <p><em>The @ menu in ChatGPT Work shows matching plugins and skills. Select a plugin under Plugins.</em></p> <p>If the plugin needs an app connection, follow the prompts to connect it. To find and install a plugin, see <a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\">Plugins</a>.</p> <h2 id=\"create-a-plugin-from-scratch\">Create a plugin from scratch</h2> <p>Start with a task you do regularly and a clear example of the result you want. Plugin Creator helps turn that description into a reusable workflow through a conversation: you can explain the steps, add a template or reference file, and refine the instructions as you go. The written example below uses a Document Summary plugin that turns a document into an overview, key points, and open questions. You can adapt the same steps to another task.</p> <p><a href=\"https://cdn.openai.com/devhub/docs/codex/build-plugins/create-plugin-2x-hq.webm\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">A plugin creation example showing an initial request and Plugin Creator’s first response, at twice the original speed. (online)</a></p> <p>This recording shows an initial plugin request and Plugin Creator’s first response. The written examples below use a separate workflow.</p> <h3 id=\"step-1-mention-plugin-creator\">Step 1: Mention Plugin Creator</h3> <p>Start a conversation in Chat or ChatGPT Work. Type <strong>@</strong>, search for <strong>Plugin Creator</strong>, and select it from the menu.</p> <h3 id=\"step-2-describe-the-workflow\">Step 2: Describe the workflow</h3> <p>A good creation prompt gives Plugin Creator a practical brief:</p> <ul> <li><strong>Purpose:</strong> Name the recurring task and when you’ll use the plugin.</li> <li><strong>Inputs:</strong> Describe the information you’ll provide and how it should use each attached file.</li> <li><strong>Output:</strong> Say who the result is for, and specify its format, length, and tone. Include an example if you have one.</li> <li><strong>Rules:</strong> Explain required steps, what needs your review, and how to handle missing information. For example, ask a question or mark a field “not specified.”</li> </ul> <p>Ask for instructions you can reuse with new inputs. Keep the details of an individual task, such as a particular document, labeled as an example for testing.</p> <p><strong>Create a plugin from scratch:</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Create a plugin called Document Summary. Summarize documents I provide in three sections: Overview, Key points, and Open questions. Use the attached template for the format. Base the summary only on the document. If requested information is missing, mark it as not provided. Do not edit the source document.\n</code></pre> <h3 id=\"step-3-add-context-and-refine-the-instructions\">Step 3: Add context and refine the instructions</h3> <p>Attach a template, example, or reference file the plugin should use. Answer Plugin Creator's questions and ask for changes until the instructions match the task. If the workflow needs an app, explain which part of the task depends on it.</p> <p>Keep the first version focused on one workflow. A clear name and description will help you and your teammates recognize when to use it.</p> <h3 id=\"step-4-review-and-finish-creating-the-plugin\">Step 4: Review and finish creating the plugin</h3> <p>Follow Plugin Creator's prompts to finish. Review the plugin's name, description, instructions, and reference material before relying on it.</p> <p>New workspace plugins start private so you can test them before sharing.</p> <h2 id=\"include-apps-in-your-plugin\">Include apps in your plugin</h2> <p>Apps connect ChatGPT to other services, such as file storage or project management tools. Depending on the app and its enabled features, ChatGPT can search or read information and may be able to take actions, such as creating a document or updating a record. Skills describe how to do the work; apps provide the information or actions it needs.</p> <p>Apps are optional. Document Summary can work with text you paste or a file you attach. Include an app if you want the workflow to retrieve a document from another service or perform a supported action there.</p> <h3 id=\"find-apps-available-to-you\">Find apps available to you</h3> <p>Browse in the workspace where you plan to create and use the plugin:</p> <ol> <li>Open <strong>Plugins</strong> in ChatGPT. Search for the service you want to use, or browse the tab with your workspace’s name.</li> <li>Open a plugin’s details and review its <strong>Apps</strong> section. A plugin may be named after the service it connects to, but some plugins contain only skills.</li> <li>Check the included app’s capabilities and connection status. Follow <strong>Connect</strong> prompts when required. If it shows <strong>Disabled by admin</strong> or <strong>Admin approval required</strong>, ask your workspace admin about access.</li> </ol> <p>If your account shows <strong>Apps</strong> instead of <strong>Plugins</strong>, browse available connections there. Seeing a plugin in the directory does not mean every included app is ready to use.</p> <p>Note the app’s name and what it supports, then tell Plugin Creator how you want to use it. For more on browsing and setup, see <a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a?anchor=use-and-install-plugins\">Plugins</a>.</p> <h3 id=\"add-an-app-to-your-workflow\">Add an app to your workflow</h3> <p>When creating or editing a plugin:</p> <ol> <li><strong>Choose an available app.</strong> Use an app your workspace allows and that you have permission to use. If it is unavailable, ask your workspace admin about access.</li> <li><strong>Explain its job.</strong> Tell Plugin Creator which app to include, what information to read or action to take, and what you want to review first.</li> <li><strong>Connect and check.</strong> Follow any setup prompts and review the requested permissions. You may need to sign in; some apps use an administrator-managed connection. Review the finished plugin’s apps, then test with information you can already access.</li> </ol> <p>In the example below, replace <strong>[app name]</strong> with an app your workspace allows.</p> <p><strong>Include an app:</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Include [app name] in Document Summary, if it’s available to me. Read the document I link to and draft the Overview, Key points, and Open questions in chat. Keep the rule about marking missing information. Do not create or edit files in the app. If you cannot access the document, ask me to attach it.\n</code></pre> <p>Including an app does not grant new access. Your workspace’s app and action settings, connection permissions, and access in the source service still apply. Teammates who use the plugin also need the required app access and connection setup.</p> <h3 id=\"connect-a-custom-mcp-server\">Connect a custom MCP server</h3> <p>If an existing app doesn’t cover your workflow, <a href=\"#/article/a-dd3c07a3ae6aafeb?sectionMissing=build-an-mcp-plugin\" title=\"旧来源章节未在本地快照中定位，打开该文章；可通过官方来源查看当前章节。\">connect your tools with a custom MCP server</a>. Use Plugin Creator and Sites to build a plugin that connects to your system.</p> <h2 id=\"test-your-plugin\">Test your plugin</h2> <p>Install the plugin if prompted, then start a new conversation. Select it with an <strong>@ mention</strong> and give it a familiar task. For Document Summary, provide a document you know well and ask for a summary.</p> <p>Check that the result follows your format, uses the right reference material, and identifies missing information. Then try a document with missing or unclear details and check that the summary identifies those gaps.</p> <p>If the plugin uses an app, check that it can access the information or actions the task requires. If you plan to use it in both Chat and Work, test it in each. Available tools and apps can differ.</p> <p>Keep a few example prompts to reuse after making changes.</p> <blockquote> <p>Illustration: Create a plugin, test it with a real example, edit its instructions or files, and test again. Return to editing and retesting as needed, then share after reviewing the results.</p> </blockquote> <p><em>Test before sharing, and repeat your checks after an update.</em></p> <h2 id=\"edit-an-existing-plugin\">Edit an existing plugin</h2> <h3 id=\"step-1-open-the-plugin-for-editing\">Step 1: Open the plugin for editing</h3> <p>Open <strong>Plugins</strong>, select the plugin you want to change, and choose <strong>Edit Plugin</strong>. This opens a conversation for updating it.</p> <h3 id=\"step-2-describe-what-should-change\">Step 2: Describe what should change</h3> <p>A good editing prompt names the behavior or reference file to update, describes the desired change, and identifies what to preserve. If a result missed the mark, include that result and explain what you expected. Ask for a sample using familiar inputs so you can compare before and after.</p> <p>Make clear whether you want to update the plugin’s reusable instructions or revise a single result. When replacing a reference file, name the old file and explain how to use the new one.</p> <p>For example, to change the output:</p> <p><strong>Update the output:</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Update Document Summary so Key points appears in a table with Point and Source columns. In Source, identify the supporting passage or section when available. Keep Overview, Open questions, and the rule about marking missing information. Show me a sample result from this document.\n</code></pre> <p>To replace reference material:</p> <p><strong>Replace reference material:</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Replace the existing summary template with the attached revised template. Keep the other reference files and instructions unchanged. Tell me what you changed, then help me test it with this document.\n</code></pre> <h3 id=\"step-3-review-the-update\">Step 3: Review the update</h3> <p>Review the revised instructions and files, then follow the prompts to complete the update. Check that the requested changes are present and that information you still need remains intact.</p> <h3 id=\"step-4-test-again\">Step 4: Test again</h3> <p>Open a new conversation and repeat your saved test prompts. Check the updated behavior and the parts of the workflow you intended to preserve. If other people use the plugin, ask a teammate to try a representative task before the wider team relies on the change.</p> <h2 id=\"share-the-plugin-with-your-team\">Share the plugin with your team</h2> <p>When the plugin is ready, use its sharing settings to choose the intended people or groups. Sharing requires <strong>Share plugins</strong> permission. Adding it to the workspace directory requires <strong>Publish plugins to workspace</strong> permission.</p> <p>Sharing and installation are separate. Recipients need to install the plugin unless an admin has already installed it for them. If the workflow uses an app, each person also needs the required app access and any account connection the app requires.</p> <p>Include a sample prompt with the plugin link and let teammates know who maintains it. See <a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\">Plugins</a> for more on installation and use.</p> <h2 id=\"if-you-cannot-create-or-edit-a-plugin\">If you cannot create or edit a plugin</h2> <p>Check that you are in the intended workspace. If the create option or plugin editor is missing, ask your workspace admin to confirm that the experience is available and that you have the access needed for the task.</p> <p>If a teammate can open the plugin but cannot use it, check plugin installation, workspace permission to use plugins, and access to required apps separately. Admins can review <a href=\"#/article/a-20bc98306a44b420\">Plugin controls</a>.</p> <h2 id=\"continue-with-the-builder-documentation\">Continue with the builder documentation</h2> <p>For custom integrations or development with plugin files, see <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/plugins/build/plugins.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Package your plugin</a>. The <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/plugins/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">developer documentation (not in this local snapshot)</a> covers building skills and MCP servers, <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/plugins/build/extensions.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">extensions</a>, testing, and public submission.</p> <p>For workspace distribution through GitHub, see <a href=\"#/article/a-ab115ea47731f92a\">Plugin management</a>.</p>"};
